ated\nrequirements. No services, deployment, extra abstractions, or speculative\nfeatures (YAGNI). For this project that means a single small module with a\nplain function, not a framework.\nRationale: scope creep is the main risk for a one-function arithmetic utility.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\nUnresolved assumptions, open questions, and any behavior regressions MUST be\nrecorded in the feature artifacts (spec/plan/tasks or a handoff note) and kept\ncurrent until resolved. A change that risks a regression MUST name the\naffected behavior and the check that guards it.\nRationale: keeps deferred work visible across phases and agents.\n\n## Scope and Non-Goals\nThe project is a minimal arithmetic utility: `smoke.py` exposing\n`add(a, b)` that returns `a + b`, supporting negative integers, zero, and\nfloats, with tests. Non-goals: any service, CLI, deployment, persistence,\nconfiguration, or modification of the upstream `tinydb` package or its tests.\nWorkflow artifacts MUST stay concise and live under\n`specs/001-transactions`.\n\n## Development Workflow\n1. Constitution governs all phases; later phases MUST check compliance.\n2. Requirements MUST be written with acceptance criteria before planning.\n3. Implementation MUST be followed by running the tests and recording the\n   command and observed result.\n4. Artifacts MUST remain concise; no placeholder-only files.\n\n## Governance\nThis constitution supersedes conflicting local practice for this feature.\nAmendments MUST update the version line using semantic versioning: MAJOR for\nremoving or redefining principles, MINOR for adding principles or materially\nexpanding guidance, PATCH for wording or non-semantic clarifications.\nCompliance is reviewed at each phase boundary; violations MUST be fixed or\ndocumented as an explicit, justified exception in the feature artifacts.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-16 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-16\n'''\nopen('.specify/memory/constitution.